===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|παραλληλεπίπεδος||with parallel surfaces}}, from {{m|grc|παράλληλος||parallel}} + {{m|grc|ἐπίπεδος||plane}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpæɹəˌlɛləˈpaɪpɪd/|/ˌpæɹəlɛlˈɛpɪpɛd/}}
* {{audio|en|En-ca-parallelepiped.opus|Audio (CA)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|geometry}} A solid figure, having six faces, all [[parallelogram]]s; all opposite faces being similar and [[parallel]].
#: {{ux|en|A cuboid is a rectangular '''parallelepiped'''.}}

